# A CRLF shebang is not a shebang: the kernel looks for `/bin/sh\r` and the
# container dies with a "no such file or directory" naming a file that plainly
# exists. Development is on Windows, so this is not hypothetical.
#
# Scoped deliberately to what runs inside a container. A blanket
# `* text=auto eol=lf` would renormalise every tracked file in the repo on the
# next touch, burying a real change in a whole-tree line-ending diff.

*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.Dockerfile text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
docker-compose.yml text eol=lf
docker-compose.*.yml text eol=lf
